      },
      {
        "done": true,
        "id": "place",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": true,
        "target": "box:2n2222a",
        "text": "Kit's fan board. Drag a transistor from the shoebox onto the board: the 2N2222A is rated for 600 mA, the BC547B only for 100."
      },
      {
        "done": true,
        "id": "base",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": true,
        "target": "pad:2,7",
        "text": "A resistor goes from the PIN pad to the transistor's base: it sets how much base current the pin gives."
      },
      {
        "done": true,
        "id": "wire",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": true,
        "target": "pad:22,4",
        "text": "Wire the PIN pad through the resistor to the base, the emitter to GND and the collector to the COLL pad (the fan's low end)."
      },
      {
        "done": false,
        "id": "diode",
        "optional": true,
        "shown": true,
        "target": "box:1n4007",
        "text": "A diode across the fan, its banded end on the 12 V side, gives the fan's current somewhere to go when the transistor turns off."
      },
      {
        "done": false,
        "id": "diode-burn",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": true,
        "target": "box:1n4007",
        "text": "The transistor burned when the fan switched off: a fan is a coil, and a coil's current cannot stop at once. Put a diode across the fan, its banded end on the 12 V side, before you try again. Optional: A diode across the fan, its banded end on the 12 V side, gives the fan's current somewhere to go when the transistor turns off."
      },
      {
        "done": true,
        "id": "power",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": true,
        "target": "rocker",
        "text": "Switch the bench on. The PIN switch turns the pin high, low or 100 Hz."
      },
      {
        "done": false,
        "id": "run-bench",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": true,
        "target": "bench",
        "text": "Run the bench: it tries the pin high, low and switching at 100 Hz."
      },
      {
        "done": true,
        "id": "done",
        "optional": false,
        "shown": false,
        "target": "chit",
        "text": "Kit's fan spins from a pin, and stays whole when it is switched off."
      }
    ]
